blocks.en:
Suppose there were two fixed points $x$ and $y$. Then
\begin{equation}\label{eq:banach-contraction-fixed-point-uniqueness}
d(x,y)=d(T(x),T(y))\leq\theta d(x,y),
\end{equation}
which is possible only if $x=y$.

Now consider any point $x_0\in X$ and define recursively $x_{n+1}=T(x_n)$. Then we have $d(x_{n+1},x_n)\leq\theta d(x_n,x_{n-1})$, from which it easily follows that the sequence $x_n$ is Cauchy. Let $x$ be the limit. Then we have
\begin{equation}\label{eq:banach-contraction-iteration-limit-fixed-point}
T(x)=T\left(\lim_{n\to\infty}x_n\right)=\lim_{n\to\infty}T(x_n)=\lim_{n\to\infty}x_{n+1}=x.
\end{equation}
This completes the proof.

blocks.zh:
假设有两个不动点 $x$ 和 $y$. 则
\begin{equation}\label{eq:banach-contraction-fixed-point-uniqueness}
d(x,y)=d(T(x),T(y))\leq\theta d(x,y),
\end{equation}
这只有在 $x=y$ 时才可能.

现在任取一点 $x_0\in X$, 递归定义 $x_{n+1}=T(x_n)$. 则有 $d(x_{n+1},x_n)\leq\theta d(x_n,x_{n-1})$, 由此容易得到序列 $x_n$ 是 Cauchy 序列. 设 $x$ 为极限. 则有
\begin{equation}\label{eq:banach-contraction-iteration-limit-fixed-point}
T(x)=T\left(\lim_{n\to\infty}x_n\right)=\lim_{n\to\infty}T(x_n)=\lim_{n\to\infty}x_{n+1}=x.
\end{equation}
证明完成.
